00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:50,557
I was just trying to have some fun.

257
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,660
You have my word. It's me.

258
00:18:53,060 --> 00:18:54,300
I'm Joseph Joestar.

259
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,160
I was born September 27th in 1920.

260
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:01,151
My wife's name is Susie Q, and
I collect comics as a hobby.

261
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,040
I have a question for you.

262
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:07,244
Who's the leading actress
in Tarzan the Ape Man?

263
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,440
Bo Derek.

264
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:10,157
Okay, now answer this one.

265
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:12,560
Who sang Eat It, the spoof of Beat It?

266
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:15,600
Weird Al Yankovic! Good grief.

267
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:16,920
It has to be you.

268
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:19,747
Who else would know
pointless crap like that?

269
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,080
This is Card, over!

270
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,200
It's amazing! Mr.

271
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:25,752
Joestar is back with us!

272
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,197
He's come back from the brink of death!

273
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:30,260
It's a miracle! Over!

274
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:33,040
Hear that?

275
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:36,105
You've taken back everything
you stole from us.

276
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,390
Do you?

277
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:08,320
It's finally over.

278
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:16,880
Dio took something
precious from all of us.

279
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:20,160
For a hundred years, he's
taken whatever he wanted.

280
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:23,620
His appetite for power
has been insatiable.

281
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,320
He's taken far too much.

282
00:20:26,540 --> 00:20:27,720
You realize that?

283
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:33,279
Yeah, he's taken things from us that
we'll never be able to get back.

284
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:39,204
The losses that we've endured on this
journey stretch as far as the planet itself.

285
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:42,500
But, thanks to their sacrifices,

286
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:46,114
we're here to tell the tale
and carry on in their stead.

287
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:55,460
Kakyoin, Iggy, Avdol, it's over.

288
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:09,122
So you're really going
back to France, Polnareff?

289
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:13,580
This may be a bit forward,
but your family's gone.

290
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:16,568
Why don't you come back
with me to New York?

291
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:19,350
Mr.

292
00:21:19,433 --> 00:21:20,820
Joestar, I know they're gone.

293
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:23,608
But France is the only
home I've ever known.

294
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:25,429
It's filled with memories.

295
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:28,680
It's a place I must return
to no matter where I go.

296
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:31,185
But if you ever need anything,

297
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:34,849
all you have to do is call and
I'll be there in a heartbeat.

298
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:37,067
We're gonna miss you, buddy.

299
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:44,400
It wasn't easy, that's for damn sure.

300
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:47,040
But I had a hell of a time,

301
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:50,651
and I'm lucky to have been on
this adventure with you guys.

302
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:56,080
Remember, we're a team, and
that's never going to change.

303
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:02,500
Calling all passengers for France
International Airlines, Flight 92 to Paris.

304
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,640
Please proceed to Gate 18.

305
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:07,060
Ambiento, you ornery bastard.

306
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,417
Live long and happy.

307
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:12,080
And you, as moody grandson,
you'd better not forget me.

308
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:13,360
We'll meet again.

309
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:16,497
That is, of course, if you
don't hate my guts by then.

310
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:17,800
Stubborn jackass.

311
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:22,117
We wouldn't be able to forget about
you, even if we wanted to, Polnareff.

312
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,320
You be well.

313
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:26,400
Au River.

314
00:22:27,140 --> 00:22:27,970
Yeah.

315
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,220
See you later.

316
00:22:45,240 --> 00:22:48,297
Holly, how are you sitting
up straight all of a sudden?

317
00:22:48,380 --> 00:22:50,220
I'm feeling much better.

318
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,715
I'm not sure how to put it into words.

319
00:22:52,960 --> 00:22:55,317
It's as if we could
read each other's minds.

320
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,230
What?

321
00:22:56,313 --> 00:22:58,705
Mom, I can feel that
they're coming home to us.

322
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:02,490
Holly!

323
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,600
Papa and my Jotaro!

324
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:07,720
They're coming home!

325
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:16,740
Hmm?

326
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,960
Hmm.

327
00:23:22,260 --> 00:23:23,660
Hmm.

328
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:46,040
Thank you.

329
00:24:17,020 --> 00:24:17,850
Thank you.
